ITEMS=[]
def Q(stem,key,d1,d2,d3,why):ITEMS.append((stem,[key,d1,d2,d3],why))
Q("An individual demonstrates a need for a lawful ordinary handgun for personal protection that cannot reasonably be met by other means. Which licensing category addresses that need?",
 "Section 13, self-defence","Section 15, occasional hunting","Section 17, private collection","Section 20, business purposes",
 "Section 13 concerns a firearm for self-defence, subject to its requirements. A stated need is not an automatic entitlement.")
Q("An applicant goes hunting a few weekends a year and is not claiming dedicated status. Which licensing category is relevant?",
 "Section 15, occasional use","Section 16, dedicated status","Section 13, self-defence","Section 20, business purposes",
 "Section 15 covers occasional hunting and sport-shooting. Dedicated status under section 16 needs an association declaration.")
Q("An active sport shooter applies with a declaration from an accredited sport-shooting organisation confirming qualifying membership. Which licensing category is relevant?",
 "Section 16, dedicated status","Section 15, occasional use","Section 17, private collection","Section 21, temporary authorisation",
 "Section 16 concerns dedicated hunting and dedicated sport-shooting, supported by the required association declaration.")
Q("An accredited association approves an old military rifle for its historical interest, and the applicant wants to keep it for that reason. Which category is relevant?",
 "Section 17, private collection","Section 16, dedicated hunting","Section 15, occasional sport-shooting","Section 13, self-defence",
 "Section 17 concerns firearms kept in a private collection and requires the support of an accredited collectors association.")
Q("An owner wants a current licence to continue beyond its approaching expiry date. Which process addresses that objective?",
 "Applying to renew it under section 24","Applying for a copy under section 29","Notifying a change of circumstances","Applying for a new competency certificate",
 "Renewal under section 24 deals with the continued validity of a licence that is about to expire.")
Q("A licence holder moves house while the firearm and licensing purpose stay the same. Which step specifically deals with the new place of residence?",
 "A section 25 address notification","A renewal application","A new competency application","A section 29 copy application",
 "Section 25 requires written notification of a changed physical or postal address.")
Q("Material information supplied in an application changes, but neither the physical nor the postal address changes. Which notification is relevant?",
 "A section 26 notice of changed particulars","An address notice under section 25","A renewal application under section 24","A copy request under section 29",
 "Section 26 requires notification of changes to the information submitted with the application. Section 25 covers only addresses.")
Q("A current licence card is damaged so that its details can no longer be read. The licence itself has not expired. Which application addresses the damaged card?",
 "A copy application under section 29","Renewing the licence ahead of expiry","Applying for a new licence for it","Notifying a change of particulars",
 "Section 29 provides for a copy when a document is defaced, lost or stolen. This is separate from renewing the licence.")
Q("A holder discovers that a firearm licence card has been stolen. How soon must the theft be reported to the Registrar under section 29?",
 "Within 24 hours","Within 48 hours","Within 7 days","Within 30 days",
 "The report is due within 24 hours of discovering the loss or theft. Applying for a copy is a separate duty with its own period.")
Q("A licence card has been defaced. Within what period after discovering this must the holder apply for a copy under section 29?",
 "Within 7 days","Within 24 hours","Within 14 days","Within 30 days",
 "An application for a copy must be made within 7 days of discovering the defacement, loss or theft. The 24 hour period is for reporting a loss or theft.")
Q("A licence holder changes a postal address. Within what period must written notification reach the Registrar under section 25?",
 "Within 30 days","Within 7 days","Within 14 days","At the next renewal",
 "The holder must notify the Registrar in writing within 30 days after the address changes. It is not left until renewal.")
Q("An owner wishes to renew an ordinary firearm licence. What is the statutory advance filing requirement under section 24?",
 "At least 90 days before expiry","At least 30 days before expiry","At least 60 days before expiry","Within 30 days after expiry",
 "The renewal application must be made at least 90 days before the licence expires.")
Q("Ignoring any other licensing category, what is the maximum number of section 13 self-defence licences one person may hold?",
 "One","Two","Three","Four",
 "Section 13 permits no more than one licence under that section.")
Q("A person has one section 13 licence and one section 15 licence, with no additional licences. How many more section 15 licences could fit the numerical ceiling, if all other requirements are met?",
 "Two more","One more","Three more","None",
 "A person with a section 13 licence may hold three section 15 licences. With one already held, two places remain.")
Q("A person holds one section 13 licence and no additional licences. What is the total numerical ceiling for that person's section 15 licences?",
 "Three","Two","Four","Six",
 "Section 15(3)(b) reduces the section 15 ceiling to three when the person holds a section 13 licence.")
Q("A person holds no section 13 licence and no additional licences. What is the ordinary total numerical ceiling for section 15 licences?",
 "Four","Three","Six","No fixed limit",
 "Section 15 ordinarily permits up to four licences, subject to its handgun and other restrictions.")
Q("An applicant seeks a section 12 additional licence for a firearm already licensed to someone else. What connection with that holder is required?",
 "Living on the same premises as the primary holder","Being married to or related to the primary holder","Living in the same magisterial district","Belonging to the same accredited association",
 "Section 12 additional licences depend on living on the same premises as the holder of the primary licence. Family relationship alone is not the test.")
Q("A spouse assumes that a section 12 additional licence is automatic because the primary holder already qualified. What must the spouse independently satisfy?",
 "All requirements for the issue of that licence","Only the age requirement","Nothing beyond the primary holder's consent","Only the safe storage requirement",
 "Every additional licence holder must comply with all the requirements for the issue of the relevant licence.")
Q("An applicant buys two ordinary firearms and assumes a single licence can cover both of them. What principle in section 11 corrects this?",
 "Each firearm needs its own licence","One licence covers two firearms of one calibre","One licence covers all firearms in one safe","The second firearm needs only a permit",
 "Each firearm requires a separate licence, even if a single document happens to contain more than one licence.")
Q("A company obtains a firearm licence under section 20. What must the licence state to limit how the company may use the firearm?",
 "The purpose for which it is issued","The name of every employee who may carry it","The number of rounds it may fire each year","The province where the company is registered",
 "A section 20 licence must specify the business purpose for which it is issued, and use is limited to that purpose.")
Q("A section 21 temporary authorisation allows possession only. Before the holder may lawfully use the firearm, what is needed?",
 "The Registrar's endorsement permitting use","A competency certificate for that firearm only","Written consent from the previous owner","Permission from a range officer",
 "Section 21(5) requires the Registrar's endorsement permitting use, and use must follow its conditions.")
Q("A person wants to dispose of a firearm held under a section 21 temporary authorisation. Which approval addresses disposal?",
 "The Registrar's written consent","The local DFO's verbal approval","None, since it is held only temporarily","The buyer's competency certificate alone",
 "Section 21(6) requires the Registrar's written consent for disposal, subject to any conditions imposed.")
Q("A temporary authorisation specifies where the firearm may be kept. What obligation applies for the whole temporary period?",
 "Comply with the conditions it states","Keep it anywhere the holder thinks secure","Tell the DFO only when it is moved","Reapply for the authorisation every 30 days",
 "Temporary authorisation is conditional. Failing to comply with its conditions can lead to withdrawal.")
Q("An heir wants to keep an inherited ordinary firearm permanently, rather than hold it briefly for disposal. What step is required?",
 "Apply for the appropriate licence","Register the will with the DFO","Nothing, as the estate's licence passes on","Obtain a section 21 authorisation only",
 "Section 148 requires the appropriate licence, permit or authorisation. Inheritance alone does not give the right to possess.")
Q("A police record must tell apart two firearms of the same make and model. Which detail does this?",
 "Its serial number or other mark","Its calibre and barrel length","Its licence category and number","The manufacturer's model name",
 "The manufacturer's serial number or another authorised identifying mark distinguishes one firearm from an identical one.")
Q("A DFO compares the person at the counter with the ID book and the name on the application form. Which matter is being verified?",
 "The applicant's identity","The firearm's serial number","The applicant's competency","The applicant's home address",
 "This check concerns who the applicant is, not the firearm or the applicant's competence.")
Q("A buyer presents a shop receipt but is asked for the licence, permit or authorisation covering the firearm. What legal matter is the official checking?",
 "That the buyer may legally hold it","That the price was paid in full","That the buyer now owns it outright","That the buyer's tax affairs are in order",
 "A receipt shows a transaction or ownership. Lawful possession requires the authority the Act provides, such as a licence.")
Q("A licence holder stores a friend's firearm under a written storage authorisation endorsed by a DFO. Under regulation 86(4)(a)(ii), where must that firearm be kept?",
 "In a prescribed safe at the place named in the authorisation","In any locked cupboard at the storer's own home","In a safe at the friend's own home address","At the police station of the endorsing DFO",
 "Regulation 86(4)(a)(ii) requires the firearm to be stored in a prescribed safe at the place mentioned in the written authorisation.")
Q("Under section 27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section 14 restricted-firearm self-defence licence?",
 "Two years","One year","Five years","Ten years",
 "The statutory table gives a section 14 licence a two-year period, subject to termination and renewal provisions.")
Q("Under section 27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section 13 self-defence licence?",
 "Five years","Two years","Three years","Ten years",
 "The statutory table provides five years for a section 13 licence, subject to termination or renewal.")
Q("Under section 27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section 15 occasional hunting or sport-shooting licence?",
 "Ten years","Five years","Seven years","Fifteen years",
 "The statutory period for a section 15 licence is ten years, subject to the Act's termination and renewal rules.")
Q("A visitor who is not a South African citizen asks whether the Registrar may issue them a section 21 temporary authorisation to possess a firearm. What does section 21(1) say about who may receive one?",
 "Any person, including a non-citizen","Only South African citizens","Only citizens and permanent residents","Only people who already hold a firearm licence",
 "Section 21(1) allows the Registrar to issue a temporary authorisation to possess a firearm to any person, including a non-citizen, for a period and on conditions the Registrar sets.")
Q("An applicant for dedicated hunter status needs the statutory declaration supporting their registered membership. Who supplies it, through its chairperson or written delegate?",
 "Their accredited hunting association","Any registered hunting club nearby","A professional hunting outfitter","The provincial nature conservation office",
 "Section 16 requires the declaration from the relevant accredited hunting association, not from any club or outfitter.")
Q("A dedicated sport shooter needs the section 16 membership declaration. Which organisation provides it through its authorised representative?",
 "The accredited sport-shooting body","The provincial sport department","The range where the person shoots","The Registrar's sport desk at head office",
 "The relevant accredited sport-shooting organisation supplies the declaration for dedicated sport status.")
Q("A private collector needs the statutory declaration supporting collector status and the approved collection interest. Which organisation is relevant?",
 "The accredited collectors association","A licensed dealer who values the firearm","A museum curator","A collectors' club that is not accredited",
 "The accredited collectors association provides the support section 17 requires. A club without accreditation cannot.")
Q("A security officer is issued a company firearm for authorised work. Which entity must hold the business firearm licence and ensure the officer has the required competency?",
 "The security firm that employs the officer","The security officer in their own name","The client whose site is being guarded","The private security industry regulator",
 "Section 20 requires the security service provider that holds the business licence to supply the firearm only to a competent security officer in its service, subject to the prescribed conditions.")
Q("A relative offers an ordinary firearm as a gift. The recipient has no licence, permit, authorisation or other permission for it. What must come first?",
 "Obtaining lawful authority first","Taking it home, then applying within 30 days","A signed deed of donation","Nothing, since it is a family gift",
 "A gift does not override the general prohibition on possession. The recipient must obtain the appropriate legal authority before taking possession.")
Q("A newly issued licence contains a clerical mistake. What should the holder do instead of changing the printed details personally?",
 "Apply to correct it via the DFO","Correct it neatly in ink","Leave it until the next renewal","Ask the selling dealer to amend it",
 "Regulation 108 provides a prescribed correction application through the DFO. Altering a licence without authority is prohibited.")
Q("An owner discovers that the serial number on a firearm has worn away so that it can no longer be read, without having altered it. What is required?",
 "Notify the Registrar forthwith","Re-stamp the number themselves","Wait until the next renewal","Report it within 30 days",
 "Section 23(6) requires notification to the Registrar forthwith when the identifying mark has become illegible or has been tampered with.")
Q("A section 12 holder has moved away from the primary licence holder's premises and the additional licence has lapsed. What must be done with that document?",
 "Return it to the Registrar at once","Keep it until its expiry date","Hand it to the primary holder","Destroy it and keep a written record",
 "Section 12 requires the lapsed additional licence to be returned to the Registrar forthwith.")
Q("A company nominates a new competent responsible person under section 7. Within what period from nomination must it notify the Registrar?",
 "Within seven days","Within 24 hours","Within 30 days","Within 90 days",
 "Section 7(4) requires written notification within seven days of the nomination.")
Q("Before the Registrar may issue a section 28(2) cancellation notice, how much written notice to submit representations does section 28(3)(a) require?",
 "Thirty days","Seven days","Fourteen days","Sixty days",
 "Section 28(3)(a) requires the Registrar to give the holder 30 days' notice in writing to submit written representations before a cancellation notice under section 28(2) may be issued.")
Q("After receiving a section 28 cancellation notice, what is the ordinary period for disposing of the firearm through a dealer or as the Registrar determines, absent an extension?",
 "Sixty days","Thirty days","Ninety days","Six months",
 "Section 28(4) provides sixty days after receipt of the notice, with a possible extension on good cause.")
Q("An association's accreditation under the relevant section 8 provision is cancelled and notice is published in the Gazette. Within what period must its members join another relevant accredited association?",
 "Six months","Sixty days","Thirty days","Twelve months",
 "Section 8(4)(a) gives members six months from publication of the notice to join another relevant accredited body. Sixty days is the disposal period after a licence cancellation.")
Q("An accreditation review investigates whether an organisation's officers keep honest records and act reliably. Which statutory criterion most directly concerns that evidence?",
 "Trustworthiness and integrity","Annual financial turnover","Size of its membership","Number of shooting ranges it owns",
 "Section 8 includes trustworthiness and integrity among the minimum accreditation criteria. Size and turnover are not listed criteria.")
Q("An accreditation review asks whether an organisation is appropriate to perform the particular statutory role it seeks. Which criterion is directly being assessed?",
 "Suitability for the relevant functions","Trustworthiness of its officers","Length of time it has been operating","How widely its members are spread",
 "Suitability to perform the relevant functions is a separate criterion from honesty or resources.")
Q("An organisation seeks recognition for a role but lacks the staff and systems needed to carry it out. Which accreditation criterion most directly concerns this shortfall?",
 "Capacity to serve its purpose","Integrity of its officers","Its tax compliance status","Suitability for a different role",
 "Capacity to serve the purpose of the accreditation concerns whether the organisation can actually do the work.")
Q("A proposed accredited organisation can run its own events but has no ability to support the broader statutory objectives of lawful control. Which criterion is specifically in question?",
 "Capacity to advance the Act's purposes","Capacity to run its own events","Trustworthiness of its chairperson","Suitability of its premises",
 "Section 8 also requires capacity to advance the purposes of the Act, beyond running the organisation's own activities.")
Q("Ownership passes to another person in exchange for an agreed price. Which form of transfer under the Act is described?",
 "A sale","A donation","A loan","A rental",
 "Selling is included in the statutory definition of transfer. Payment does not remove the lawful-possession requirements.")
Q("A person gives a firearm to another without receiving payment and intends the recipient to keep it. Which form of transfer is described?",
 "A donation","A sale on credit","A loan","A rental",
 "A donation is a transfer under the Act and still requires lawful authority for possession.")
Q("An owner hands over a firearm for a while without any charge, expecting it back. Which form of transfer is described?",
 "A loan","A rental","A donation","A sale with a buy-back",
 "Lending is included in transfer. The owner keeping ownership does not remove the Act's requirements.")
Q("A person hands over a firearm for an agreed period in return for a fee. Which form of transfer is described?",
 "Letting, that is a rental","A free loan","A sale","A donation with conditions",
 "Letting is included in transfer. A hire arrangement cannot replace the legally required authority.")
Q("A trust deed describes the trust's charitable goals but says nothing allowing it to hold weapons or ammunition. Which section 7 element is missing?",
 "A clause authorising it to hold firearms","A clause listing each firearm's value","A clause naming who inherits the firearms","A clause naming the trust's auditors",
 "The deed must clearly provide for possession of the relevant firearms, ammunition or muzzle loading firearms.")
Q("A trust deed allows the trust to hold firearms but does not say why the trust would hold them. Which required element is missing?",
 "Why the trust will hold them","A list of the trust's beneficiaries","The date the trust was registered","The trust's bank details",
 "The deed must clearly state the intended purpose of possession.")
Q("A trust deed allows the trust to hold firearms for a stated purpose but places no limit at all on how long it may hold them. Which required element is missing?",
 "A clause ending possession once the purpose no longer requires it","A clause fixing a ten-year end date for possession","A clause requiring the firearms to be insured","A clause requiring every trustee to be a dedicated hunter",
 "Section 7 requires that possession last only while it is necessary to achieve the stated intended purpose.")
Q("A company has completed its internal approval but has not identified anyone to make its firearm application on its behalf. What appointment is still required?",
 "A natural person to act for it","A juristic person as guarantor","An accredited association as sponsor","An auditor to sign the application",
 "A juristic applicant must nominate a natural person to act as its responsible person under section 7.")
Q("An appeal notice says the applicant disagrees with the Registrar but does not say what was refused or cancelled. Which required element is missing?",
 "The decision being challenged","A sworn affidavit by the DFO","A copy of the competency certificate","A letter from a legal representative",
 "Regulation 91 requires the notice to identify the decision being appealed.")
Q("An appeal notice identifies the refusal and explains the objection but omits when the Registrar ruled. Which required element is missing?",
 "The date of the decision","The appellant's date of birth","The firearm's date of purchase","The licence's expiry date",
 "The date of the decision must be stated. It matters for the appeal period.")
Q("An appeal notice identifies a decision and its date but gives no reasons why it should be changed. Which required element is missing?",
 "The grounds relied on","A list of the appellant's other firearms","The DFO's comments on the case","A request for legal costs",
 "The notice must clearly state the ground or grounds of appeal.")
Q("An appellant has drafted separate written arguments supporting the appeal but has not included them with the notice. What required step remains?",
 "Attach them to the notice","Send them once the notice is acknowledged","Send them to the DFO some weeks later","Read them out at the hearing instead",
 "Regulation 91 requires supporting written submissions to accompany the appeal notice.")
assert len(ITEMS)==60
